      "text": "To find the remainder when the sum of the arithmetic sequence \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6, we first need to determine the number of terms in the sequence and then find the sum of the sequence. Finally, we will compute the remainder when this sum is divided by 6.\n\nThe given sequence is an arithmetic sequence where the first term \\(a = 1\\) and the common difference \\(d = 6\\). The \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[ a_n = a + (n-1)d \\]\nWe need to find the number of terms \\(n\\) in the sequence. The last term of the sequence is 259. So, we set up the equation:\n\\[ 259 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6 \\]\nSolving for \\(n\\):\n\\[ 259 = 1 + 6n - 6 \\]\n\\[ 259 = 6n - 5 \\]\n\\[ 264 = 6n \\]\n\\[ n = 44 \\]\nSo, there are 44 terms in the sequence.\n\nThe sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[ S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a + l) \\]\nwhere \\(l\\) is the last term. Substituting the known values:\n\\[ S_{44} = \\frac{44}{2} (1 + 259) = 22 \\cdot 260 = 5720 \\]\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6. We do this by computing the remainder of 5720 when divided by 6:\n\\[ 5720 \\div 6 = 953 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\nSo, the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6 is 2. Therefore, the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6 is:\n\\[ \\boxed{2} \\]",
