      "text": "To determine the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6, we start by identifying the sequence and its properties.\n\nThe sequence given is an arithmetic sequence where the first term \\(a = 1\\) and the common difference \\(d = 6\\). The general form of the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[\na_n = a + (n-1)d\n\\]\nWe need to find the number of terms \\(n\\) in the sequence. The last term of the sequence is 259. Setting \\(a_n = 259\\), we have:\n\\[\n259 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6\n\\]\nSolving for \\(n\\):\n\\[\n259 = 1 + 6(n-1) \\implies 258 = 6(n-1) \\implies n-1 = 43 \\implies n = 44\n\\]\nSo, there are 44 terms in the sequence.\n\nNext, we calculate the sum of the arithmetic sequence. The sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[\nS_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a + l)\n\\]\nwhere \\(l\\) is the last term. Substituting the known values:\n\\[\nS_{44} = \\frac{44}{2} (1 + 259) = 22 \\cdot 260 = 5720\n\\]\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6. We do this by finding the remainder of 5720 when divided by 6:\n\\[\n5720 \\div 6 = 953 \\text{ remainder } 2\n\\]\nSo, the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6 is 2. Therefore, the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6 is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
